BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Resilience in the Time We Are Living Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T143000
UID:69fe2ff0e8af4a2f007123b1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​This presentation will discuss a clear definition of resili
 ence\, how to adapt and deal with life's challenges\, share the 4 phases o
 f resilience\, provide tips and tools to improve mental well-being and how
  to set goals that can be applied to challenging situations which will enh
 ance resiliency.\nParticipants can expect to gain an understanding of resi
 lience and how to apply it to their lives and challenges. We will discuss 
 the importance of identifying daily steps that will produce positive outco
 mes and begin to heal and grow new pathways with time and repetition.\nPre
 sented by retired City of Toronto social workers\, Jill Kumer and Bryna W
 asserman.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe2ff0e8af4a2f007123b1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vegetarian Sushi Making for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T153000
UID:69fb77cde8af4a2f00709b04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TV host and celebrity chef Sang Kim will teach the basics of s
 ushi making. Participants will make sushi rolls using ingredients prepared
  by the Chef and eat their own creations. A brief history of sushi\, its o
 rigins and eating etiquette will also be shared.\nSpace is limited.\nTicke
 ts will be handed out 30 minutes prior to start time.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb77cde8af4a2f00709b04
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T150000
UID:6a14b5f94dc267647daa9e13@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun filled afternoon of activities\, arts and cr
 afts\, games and great conversation. Whether you’d like to get creative\
 , share a laugh\, or simply enjoy some friendly company\, this is the perf
 ect place to be.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, This program will take place in the program r
 oom.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a14b5f94dc267647daa9e13
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Newcomer Seniors' Wellness Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T123000
UID:69629af776261f280063a66a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is run by the Library Settlement Partnership (LSP
 ) and will focus on:\nLearning simple everyday English\nLearning basic com
 puter and email skills\nMaking new friends and expanding your social circl
 e\nThis program will be presented in English and Mandarin. For registrati
 on and enquiries\, please contact Wen at 647-388-3762 or email wchen@ccsca
 n.ca\nIn partnership with Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, 
 Catholic Crosscultural Services & Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room\, First Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69629af776261f280063a66a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Microsoft Office Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T153000
UID:69fd0bf6caf93436005a7dae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:*PARTICIPANTS MUST HAVE MOUSE AND KEYBOARDING SKILLS*\nThese i
 ntroductory courses are for beginners. Join us in the Microsoft Office Bas
 ics series where we will learn how to work with Microsoft Word\, Excel and
  PowerPoint.\nParticipants will learn how to use basic functions including
  how to create\, save and open documents. As classes progress\, learners w
 ill build on their skills to use even more tools to design their documents
 \, spreadsheets and PowerPoint presentations.\nCourse schedule:\nJun 15th 
 : Microsoft Word 1 : Write a Letter\nJun 22nd : Microsoft Word 2 : Create 
 a Flyer\nJun 29th : Microsoft Word 3 : Craft a Resume\nJul 6th: PowerPoint
  1\nJul 13th: Excel 1 : Create a Spreadsheet\nJul 20th: Excel 2 Do more wi
 th your data
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd0bf6caf93436005a7dae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
