DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T150000
UID:6a14b5f94dc267647daa9e15@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun filled afternoon of activities\, arts and cr
 afts\, games and great conversation. Whether you’d like to get creative\
 , share a laugh\, or simply enjoy some friendly company\, this is the perf
 ect place to be.
LOCATION:Junction Triangle\, This program will take place in the program r
 oom.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a14b5f94dc267647daa9e15
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors Social Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T120000
UID:6a1da22f90cc4e3a790a863f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all Seniors! Whether you are looking for a place to re
 lax\, play some board & card games\, or to just meet other people to talk 
 about sports and politics (or whatever tickles your fancy)\, join us for o
 ur Seniors Social Club!\nThis is a\ndrop-in program\nfor Older Adults. No 
 registration required.\nEvery Friday from 11:00 am - 12:00 pm.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1da22f90cc4e3a790a863f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T160000
UID:69e14588129f12743838ff01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nRise of the Superstorms\nIn the span of a sin
 gle\, catastrophic month\, Houston\, Florida\, and the Caribbean were perm
 anently altered. During the summer of 2017\, three massive hurricanes barr
 elled in from the Atlantic in rapid succession\, smashing long-standing re
 cords and claiming hundreds of lives. Closed Captions. 60 minutes. 2018
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e14588129f12743838ff01
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Not Without Hope
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T150000
UID:6a1b2a48c7d3cd58005ce3b3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of Not Without Hope movie.\nBased on a true story\, friends Nick\, Will\,
  Marquis\, and Corey's boat capsizes in the Gulf of Mexico. Battling storm
 s\, sharks\, and hypothermia\, they fight to survive as the Coast Guard mo
 unts a daring rescue to bring them home.\nRated 14A. 2hr.\nEnglish Subtitl
 es for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1b2a48c7d3cd58005ce3b3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
