BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Afternoon Movie - Downton Abbey\, The Grand Finale (2025)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T160000
UID:69e63ec9bd5c392c76455672@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When Lady Mary (Michelle Dockery) finds herself at the center 
 of a public scandal and the family faces financial trouble\, the household
  grapples with the threat of social disgrace. The Crawleys must embrace ch
 ange with the next generation leading Downton Abbey into the future.\nPG\,
  123 minutes\n**Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when avai
 lable.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e63ec9bd5c392c76455672
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 3: PivotTables & Conditional Formatting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T153000
UID:6a1863eef56bd86e00b2bf07@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills and learn to use Ex
 cel data effectively.\nIn this third session\, you will:\nUse Conditional 
 Formatting to visualize data\nExplore the power of PivotTables for data su
 mmary and analysis\nSort and filter the data in tables and using slicers\n
 Take home practice data to improve your new skills\nUpon completion of thi
 s class\, you will be able to get more from your data using Pivot tables.\
 nPrerequisites:  Excel Basics 1 and 2 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse
  and keyboard skills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1863eef56bd86e00b2bf07
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Managing Your Finances in Retirement.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T150000
UID:6a10c59dc6a1dc3d00d58a57@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for these managing finances lecture in retirement\, ho
 sted by Heather Walsh.\nHeather is a retired accountant who has been volu
 nteering with CPA Canada’s Financial Literacy program since 2015.\nThis 
 lecture is designed to empower seniors in managing their finances during r
 etirement. Learn essential strategies for budgeting\, saving\, and plannin
 g for a secure financial future. Whether you are just starting to think ab
 out retirement or are looking for ways to improve your financial health.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10c59dc6a1dc3d00d58a57
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
