BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Film Club Presents: Wicked
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T200000
UID:69fd1138703c336300262c78@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a monthly film screening of\nWicked\n(2024\, Rated
  PG).\nWicked\, the untold story of the witches of Oz\, a young woman\, mi
 sunderstood because of her unusual green skin\, who has yet to discover he
 r true power\, and Glinda\, a popular young woman\, gilded by privilege an
 d ambition\, who has yet to discover her true heart.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd1138703c336300262c78
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Film Club Presents: Saturday Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T200000
UID:69fd15ecc7d3cd580057bf67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a monthly film screening of\nSaturday Night\n(2024
 \, Rated R).\nAt 11:30 pm on October 11\, 1975\, a ferocious troupe of you
 ng comedians and writers changed television\, and culture\, forever. This 
 film is based on the true story of what happened behind the scenes in the 
 90 minutes leading up to the first broadcast of Saturday Night Live.\nDrop
 -in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd15ecc7d3cd580057bf67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
