DESCRIPTION:Join us for presentations\non Italian Heritage Month and Osteo
 porosis\, these\nevents are designed to support seniors in our community.\
 nViviana Filazzola\, COSTI Elderly Persons’ Centre Co-ordinator\, will s
 hare information on community programs and benefits available to seniors. 
 You will learn about tips for maintaining wellness and social connection\,
  information on pensions\, health services\, local supports and how to acc
 ess resources in your community.\nMondays\nJune 8 – Italian Heritage Mon
 th\nJune 22 – Osteoporosis
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Auditorium\, Lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe3b3bf6bd012f0066a193
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renoviction and Resistance in the Capitalist City-Author Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260707T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260707T200000
UID:6a04c670177319280019832d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:There's a lot of money to be made through eviction\, which is
  why landlords draw from a playbook of legal and extra-legal tactics to r
 enovict tenants.\nIn\nRenoviction and Resistance in the Capitalist City\n\
 , Cole Webber and Philip Zigman analyze how and why landlords renovict ten
 ants\, share real-life examples of tenants who have organized to fight bac
 k and kept their homes in the face of landlords’ attempts to renovict th
 em\, and discuss how municipal bylaws actually legitimize the practice rat
 her than prevent displacement.\nQ&A and discussion to follow.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st floor\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04c670177319280019832d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
