BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T153000
UID:69fa1b2000c14247035ae813@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 222
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa1b2000c14247035ae813
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of Classical Violin and Cello Duets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T200000
UID:6a0fa0a1fab4ff0f649acfd1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Annette Street Library for an engaging evening 
 of live music and conversation. This recital features Susan Spier violin\,
  and Tova Rosenberg cello\, performing works by composers who shaped music
  across different time periods\, and including Vivaldi\, Beethoven\, and R
 avel. The program will feature brief\, accessible commentary offering insi
 ght into the music and composers. Following the performance\, there will b
 e a Q&A session. Whether you're a long-time classical music fan or just cu
 rious to learn more\, this is a welcoming opportunity to experience great 
 music up close.\nDrop-in. No registration required
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0fa0a1fab4ff0f649acfd1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
