BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:City of Toronto Open Data Jam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
UID:6a186300bd892a0672e60538@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the possibilities of open data at the City of Toronto'
 s Open Data Jam. Connect with fellow open data enthusiasts\, discover com
 munity projects\, learn about TPL's open data resources\, and share ideas 
 that can help strengthen municipal open data initiatives. Whether you're a
 n experienced data user or just curious to learn more\, this event is a ch
 ance to make connections\, exchange ideas\, and be inspired by what's poss
 ible with open data.\nRegistration is required.\n***\nCity of Toronto Open
  Data Jams\nThe City of Toronto hosts an ongoing monthly event that spotli
 ghts Open Data.\nEach jam has a theme or topic\, ranging from user groups 
 (e.g.\, technologists\, journalists) to divisional partners (e.g.\, transp
 ortation\, public health) to areas of the City (e.g.\, Scarborough\, North
  York).\nInformation Collection Notice\n:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-3975981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\,1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a186300bd892a0672e60538
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
