BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culture and Technology Book Club : Knowing What We Know
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T200000
UID:6a1e1c3a40f528ac04dfc445@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Culture and Technology Book club brings readers together o
 nce a month to discuss new and classic texts that raise important question
 s about the way technology transforms our cultural and political lives.\nT
 his month we'll discuss:\nKnowing What We Know by Simon Winchester\nTechno
 logies of knowledge transmission and preservation have evolved throughout 
 human history. Acclaimed journalist and writer Simon Winchester attempts a
  survey of the colossal question of just how humans have come to know thin
 gs and interrogates how much continuity exists between older and contempor
 ary conceptions of knowledge.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Elearning Lab (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1e1c3a40f528ac04dfc445
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
