SUMMARY:Against the Odds: The life and times of an accidental politician
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T150000
UID:69f793a0129f1274383c6d2a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore civility in politics with Former Speaker of the Ontari
 o Legislature\, David William Warner. The author will discuss his politica
 l memoir\,\n"Against the odds: the life and times of an accidental politic
 ian"\n. What were the factors from childhood which led to a political care
 er? What were his achievements? What role in society should a retired poli
 tician play? Notably\, how do we achieve civility in politics?\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f793a0129f1274383c6d2a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
