BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lights\, Camera…It’s Never Too Late!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T120000
UID:69ef97c3c1cf6f9a7588312d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:June is Seniors Month!\nThis engaging 90-minute older adult-f
 ocused workshop breaking down the four phases of filmmaking: pre-productio
 n\, production\, post-production\, and marketing/distribution. Using real-
 world indie success stories\, participants will learn how films are develo
 ped\, shot\, edited\, and brought to audiences worldwide — proving that 
 creativity\, strategy\, and passion can turn even the smallest idea into a
  global project.\nNo film experience required!\nPresented by Sean Cistern
 a\, award-winning filmmaker\, pioneers filmmaking workshops for seniors 65
 +. He leads sessions across Canada\, including Ontario retirement communit
 ies and festivals\, using accessible tools to spark creativity\, reduce is
 olation\, and build social bonds. He is the director of the new documentar
 y\,\nSilver Screamers\n\, opening at Toronto's Hot Docs Cinema on April 3\
 , 2026. His past films include\nFrom the Vine\n\, Kiss and Cry\, and Full
  Out.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview\, Auditorium\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ef97c3c1cf6f9a7588312d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T113000
UID:69fcca4dc6a1dc3d00d2267e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.\nComputers
  for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard\nA class on basic keyboard functions fo
 r absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nIn this secon
 d session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself through practice with the most e
 ssential keyboard functions (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice 
 proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completion of this class students will be
  able to use a keyboard at a beginner level and know how to go online for 
 additional practice.\nComputers for Beginners 3: Use the Internet\nAn intr
 oductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners with little computer
  experience.\nIn this fourth session you will:\nUnderstand how to read a w
 eb site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for information usin
 g a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand its key comp
 onents\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use the int
 ernet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nComputers for Beg
 inners 4: Use Google Search and Maps\nA class on using Google's filters\, 
 tools\, and Maps for absolute beginners with little computer experience.\n
 In this fifth session you will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively 
 to find websites\, images\, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find ad
 dresses and get directions for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion o
 f this class students will be able to use more advanced search engine feat
 ures and use Google Maps at a basic level.\nComputers for Beginners 5: Use
  Windows\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginners
  with little computer experience.\nIn this third session you will:\nBecome
  familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common Wi
 ndows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applications
 \nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding o
 f how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcca4dc6a1dc3d00d2267e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T113000
UID:69fcca4dc6a1dc3d00d22680@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse\nA class on how to us
 e a mouse for absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nI
 n this first session you will:\nObserve and practice how to operate a mous
 e effectively\nUnderstand various mouse pointers and cursors\nReview basic
  keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for basic Windows functions\nUpon compl
 etion of this class students will be able to use a computer mouse at a bas
 ic level and will be able to go online for additional practice.\nComputers
  for Beginners 2: Use the Keyboard\nA class on basic keyboard functions fo
 r absolute beginners with little or no computer experience.\nIn this secon
 d session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself through practice with the most e
 ssential keyboard functions (alphabet\, number and symbol keys)\nPractice 
 proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completion of this class students will be
  able to use a keyboard at a beginner level and know how to go online for 
 additional practice.\nComputers for Beginners 3: Use the Internet\nAn intr
 oductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners with little computer
  experience.\nIn this fourth session you will:\nUnderstand how to read a w
 eb site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for information usin
 g a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand its key comp
 onents\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use the int
 ernet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nComputers for Beg
 inners 4: Use Google Search and Maps\nA class on using Google's filters\, 
 tools\, and Maps for absolute beginners with little computer experience.\n
 In this fifth session you will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively 
 to find websites\, images\, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find ad
 dresses and get directions for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion o
 f this class students will be able to use more advanced search engine feat
 ures and use Google Maps at a basic level.\nComputers for Beginners 5: Use
  Windows\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginners
  with little computer experience.\nIn this third session you will:\nBecome
  familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common Wi
 ndows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applications
 \nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding o
 f how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.
LOCATION:McGregor Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcca4dc6a1dc3d00d22680
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Night moves
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T150000
UID:69f121132866a5b4884b7107@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of Night moves movie.\nL.A. detective Harry Moseby has problems. Missing p
 ersons and bedroom stakeouts are no match for his glory days as a pro foot
 ball player. His wife is having a not-so-secret affair. And while sorting 
 things out\, he takes on the case of a runaway teenager that may be a lot 
 more than he can handle.\nRated R. 1hr 39mins.\nEnglish Subtitles for the 
 Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program room. Lower level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f121132866a5b4884b7107
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
