DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T110000
UID:6a0ddc1ef6bd012f006924b6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Steps to Safety\n– A fire and fall prevention program for ol
 der adults. Learn how to stay safe at home:\nPrevent fires\nUse and place 
 smoke      & CO alarms\nPlan safe escapes      (including special needs)\n
 Stay safe in high-rise      buildings\nUnderstand causes of      home fire
 s\nReduce nuisance alarms\nKnow how and when to      call for help\nAnd mo
 re\nThis program is hosted by\nToronto Fire Services.\nDrop-in\, no regist
 ration required. Space is limited.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Program Room-FCCR
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0ddc1ef6bd012f006924b6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
