BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Sheets: An Introduction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T153000
UID:6a162d7643b41b3d006957d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Sheets can be a useful free tool when you don
 't have access to Microsoft Excel. Topics in the course include how to cre
 ate\, save & edit Google Sheets worksheets\, as well as adding & editing d
 ata in a cell\, & more.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse pad & keyboard skills 
 are required.\nThis is a User Education program for beginners to Google Sh
 eets\, on laptops.\nLaptops will be provided for use during this class.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a162d7643b41b3d006957d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Enigmatic Elders Mystery Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T150000
UID:69e14cbfbd5c392c7644b420@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is for readers who enjoy reading various types 
 of mysteries. Meetings will be held every\nthird Thursday\nof the month.\n
 Our goal is to have fun and to travel the reading journey together.\nWe wi
 ll be covering the following 3 books on the following dates:\nFurmidable F
 oes\nby Rita Mae Brown\n(June 18\, 2026)\nThe Secret\, Book & Scone Societ
 y\nby\nEllery Adams (July 16\, 2026)\nNot Dark Yet\nby\nPeter Robinson (A
 ugust 20\, 2026)\nNOTE\n:\nPlease contact us three weeks\nprior\nto the ne
 xt meeting\nif\nyou require a Large Print copy.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 3rd floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e14cbfbd5c392c7644b420
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
