BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T193000
UID:6a0f5ede278f7c2f008eb1b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a series of 6 classes which have be
 en designed to take a learner with no\, or very few skills\, from zero to 
 a solid grounding in the absolute basics. Each class is set up to connect 
 with the previous and next class in a series format.\nRegistration is requ
 ired for the series.\nJune 4: Use the Mouse\nJune 11: Use the Keyboard\nJu
 ne 18: Use the Web\nJune 25: Use Google Search and Maps\nJuly 2: Use Windo
 ws\nJuly 9: Use Email - Gmail\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f5ede278f7c2f008eb1b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
