BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music Share for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T150000
UID:6a10631543b41b3d006852dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun afternoon where participants can connect ove
 r shared musical experiences while enjoying some light refreshments. Music
  Share for Seniors staff will play your favourite songs while you share th
 e memories they inspire. Or sit back\, listen and enjoy the musical experi
 ences of those around you. Get ready to jam out while connecting with new 
 friends!\nThis program is geared towards older adults and seniors.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Bagshaw Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10631543b41b3d006852dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Fire Services: Fire Safety for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T150000
UID:6a1078f0e13d3b4603b517af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Fire Services will be stopping by to provide practical
 \, accessible fire safety education for older adults. This presentation wi
 ll cover: how to check and maintain smoke alarms\, simple steps to prevent
  fires at home\, what to do if a fire starts\, and more.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Room B
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1078f0e13d3b4603b517af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Literature Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T200000
UID:6a107f69fab4ff0f649aeb57@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Queer Literature Book Club\, where we're gathering 
 like-minded individuals to gush and gossip about 2SLBTQ+ Literature.\nJoin
  us on Friday evenings once a month for a warm and lively discussion of o
 ur selected books! All adults are welcome!\nIf you're looking to socializ
 e with your local book worms\, this is the group for you!\nThis year we wi
 ll be reading:\nJune -\nFirst meeting - Introductions\, and pick up a cop
 y of\nOpen\, Heaven\nby Sean Hewitt.\nJuly\n-\nOpen\, Heaven\nby Sean Hewi
 tt\nAugust\n-\nI Leave It Up To You\,\nby Jinwoo Chong\nSeptember\n-\nYour
  Driver is Waiting\n\, by Priya Guns\nOctober\n-\nHijab Butch Blues\,\nby 
 Lamya H\nNovember -\nShuggie Bain\,\nby Douglas Stuart\nDecember\n-\nGiova
 nni's Room\,\nby James Baldwin\nBooks will be distributed at each meeting 
 (While supplies last).\nA Library card will be required to check them out.
 \n(These titles are subject to change)
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Third Floor\, Discussion Room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a107f69fab4ff0f649aeb57
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
