SUMMARY:Seniors' Social: The Golden Paintbrush
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T120000
UID:69f3a1d066c3387a9d086775@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:June is Seniors' Month! Join us for a very special Seniors' S
 ocial\, featuring the opportunity to take part in a beginner-friendly ac
 rylic painting class where no experience is necessary—just a willingness
  to have fun and try something new. Participants will be guided step-by-s
 tep through a simple project by a supportive instructor. Learn the basics 
 of color mixing\, brush techniques\, and composition\, while creating your
  own beautiful artwork to take home. All materials—including paints\, br
 ushes\, canvases\, and aprons—will be provided by the presenter. Just br
 ing your creativity and a smile!\nSeniors' social features fun activities
 \, great conversations\, and the chance to meet new friends! Whether you w
 ant to chat\, play a game\, or just enjoy a cup of tea and good conversati
 on\, this is the perfect place to be! Come make memories and new friends. 
 See you there!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Goldhawk Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3a1d066c3387a9d086775
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
