BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T200000
UID:6a1724ed8ea300e26318dff1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 w​​omen and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a 
 fragility fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Os
 teoporosis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your 
 risk of osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWh
 at you need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fractu
 ring a bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical
  activity\nFall prevention\nAttendees can expect to come away with fundame
 ntal knowledge about how to improve their bone health and reduce the risk 
 of developing osteoporosis
LOCATION:Deer Park\, upstairs in room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1724ed8ea300e26318dff1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
