BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alderwood Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
UID:6a17680646d5f64f7dcd1b5d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The book club title for June  is\nIn the Upper Country\nby Ka
 i Thomas. In 1859 Ontario\, an old woman arrives via the Underground Railr
 oad and is arrested for killing a white slave hunter. Instead of fleeing b
 efore the authorities can arrive\, the woman proposes a barter with a jour
 nalist: a story for a story.\n"\nIn The Upper Country\nweaves together un
 likely stories of love\, survival\, and family upheaval."\nRegular and Lar
 ge Print editions are available at Alderwood Branch for anyone joining the
  discussion group. Ebook and eAudiobook version available from tpl.ca
LOCATION:Alderwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a17680646d5f64f7dcd1b5d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
